# Core Rules

- Use TypeScript exclusively.
- Follow Clean Code principles.
- Keep components small and focused.
- Keep functions small and focused.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Avoid duplicated logic.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions.
- Avoid premature optimization.
- Never use `any` unless strictly unavoidable.
- Do not use magic numbers or magic strings.
- Use meaningful names.
- Do not leave dead code.
- Do not leave commented-out code.
- Do not duplicate existing functionality.
- Before creating a new component, hook, utility or service, check whether an existing implementation can be reused.
- Do not refactor unrelated code while implementing a feature.
- Do not modify configuration unless required.
- Do not install dependencies unless necessary.
- Do not implement backend functionality.
- Do not implement authentication.
- Do not implement remote synchronization.
- Do not implement REST API integration in the MVP.

When a requirement is ambiguous, prefer the smallest maintainable solution.